cells wrong; repaired build **27/27**, 0 of 495. `HEAD` reproduces `M_ORIG` exactly, failing set
identical. Each of the four edits has its own mutant and each is killed.

## SETTLED — cite rather than re-derive

* Book I `:578` defines `MASK` as *"1s in positions x through y (wrapping if x > y)"*; `:6882` of the
  PEM says *"It is not possible to specify an all-zero mask."*
* I verified the proposed loop offline over **all 4096** `(MB,SH)` pairs: every pair terminates,
  matches `MASK(MB, 63-SH)`, and visits each set position exactly once.
* `MODE_uint_t` is `uint64_t` in the 64-bit compilation, `uint32_t` in the 32-bit one; the file is
  compiled twice.

## QUESTIONS

1. **Is there an input on which this diff is WRONG?** Not weaker — wrong. Include `SH = 0`,
   `MB = 0`, `MB = 63`, `SH = 63`, and the `MB == 63-SH` boundary where the mask is a single bit.
