8545-
8546-B.2.4 Branch Prediction
8547-
8548-Software can use the "at" bits of Branch Conditional instructions to provide a hint to the processor about the
8549-behavior of the branch. If, for a given such instruction, the branch is almost always taken or almost always not
8550-taken, a suffix can be added to the mnemonic indicating the value to be used for the "at" bits.
8551-+ Predict branch to be taken (at=0b11)
8552-- Predict branch not to be taken (at=0b10)
8553-Such a suffix can be added to any Branch Conditional mnemonic, either basic or extended, that tests either the
8554-Count Register or a CR bit (but not both). Assemblers should use 0b00 as the default value for the " a t " bits,
8555-indicating that software has offered no prediction.
8556-
8557-Examples
8558-
8559: 1. Branch if CR0 reflects condition "less than", specifying that the branch should be predicted to be taken.
8560-         b l t + target
8561-
8562- 2. Same as (1), but target address is in the Link Register and the branch should be predicted not to be taken.
8563-         bltlr-
8564-
8565-146 PowerPC User Instruction Set Architecture
8566-Version 2.01
8567-
8568-B.3 Condition Register Logical Mnemonics
8569-
8570-The Condition Register Logical instructions can be used to set (to 1), clear (to 0), copy, or invert a given Condition
8571-Register bit. Extended mnemonics are provided that allow these operations to be coded easily.
8572-
8573-Table 5. Condition Register logical mnemonics
--
8579-Condition Register clear                       crclr bx               crnor bx,by,by
8580-
8581-Condition Register move                        crmove bx,by
8582-
8583-Condition Register not                         crnot bx,by
8584-
8585-The symbols defined in Section B.1 can be used to identify the Condition Register bits.
8586-
8587-Examples
8588-
8589-1. Set CR bit 25.
8590-
8591-crset 25                                             (equivalent to:  creqv 25,25,25)
8592-
8593:2. Clear the SO bit of CR0.
8594-
8595-crclr so                                             (equivalent to:  crxor 3,3,3)
8596-
8597-3. Same as (2), but SO bit to be cleared is in CR3.
8598-
8599-crclr 4*cr3+so                                       (equivalent to:  crxor 15,15,15)
8600-
8601-4. Invert the EQ bit.
8602-
8603-crnot eq,eq                                          (equivalent to:  crnor 2,2,2)
8604-
8605-5. Same as (4), but EQ bit to be inverted is in CR4, and the result is to be placed into the EQ bit of CR5.
8606-
8607-crnot 4*cr5+eq,4*cr4+eq                              (equivalent to:  crnor 22,18,18)
