8635-B.5 Compare Mnemonics
8636-
8637-The L field in the fixed-point Compare instructions controls whether the operands are treated as 64-bit quantities
8638-or as 32-bit quantities. Extended mnemonics are provided that represent the L value in the mnemonic rather than
8639-requiring it to be coded as a numeric operand.
8640-
8641:The BF field can be omitted if the result of the comparison is to be placed into CR Field 0. Otherwise the target
8642-CR field must be specified as the first operand. One of the CR field symbols defined in Section B.1 can be used
8643-for this operand.
8644-
8645-Note: The basic Compare mnemonics of PowerPC are the same as those of POWER, but the POWER instructions
8646-have three operands while the PowerPC instructions have four. The Assembler will recognize a basic Compare
8647-mnemonic with three operands as the POWER form, and will generate the instruction with L = 0 . (Thus the Assem-
8648:bler must require that the BF field, which normally can be omitted when CR Field 0 is the target, be specified
8649-explicitly if L is.)
8650-
