codex
The repaired handler preserves `sh` and captures the source before either destination write, including when `RA == RS`. The decoder checks `cpu->cd.ppc.bits == 32`; there is no `MODE32` exclusion around this handler. I’m checking the manual’s distinction between processor width and execution mode. The CR0 helper’s definition is outside the two permitted files.
