The candidate changes split as follows: (a) runs forever at `SH=0`; (b) and (c) are equivalent over the decoded range; (d) reads an uninitialized `n`. The unchanged CR0 call can receive a different value after repair: with `MB=0`, `SH=1`, source `0`, and old destination `1`, the old result is `0` and the repaired result is `1`.
